WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.093
<v Examiner>Three marks.

2
00:00:02.093 --> 00:00:07.042
<v Examiner>Define drug dependence and drug addiction, and explain the difference, with an example.

3
00:00:07.492 --> 00:00:10.997
Joan corrected this one in class, so use her version.

4
00:00:10.997 --> 00:00:16.220
Dependence is experiencing withdrawal symptoms when a drug is stopped abruptly.

5
00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:20.584
It can happen with a prescribed medicine taken exactly as charted,

6
00:00:20.584 --> 00:00:22.171
like a long-term opioid.

7
00:00:22.171 --> 00:00:24.486
Addiction is a behavioural pattern:

8
00:00:24.486 --> 00:00:29.445
an overwhelming involvement in getting the drug and using it, with craving,

9
00:00:29.445 --> 00:00:33.677
loss of control, use despite harm, and a high chance of relapse.

10
00:00:34.127 --> 00:00:39.294
The difference: dependence is the body's adaptation, and it can be entirely medical.

11
00:00:39.294 --> 00:00:40.955
Addiction is the behaviour.

12
00:00:40.955 --> 00:00:46.184
Her formative example: Sione won't take his analgesic because he's afraid of becoming

13
00:00:46.184 --> 00:00:46.799
dependent.

14
00:00:46.799 --> 00:00:51.105
You explain that dependence means withdrawal if it's stopped suddenly,

15
00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:55.780
which is why it's reduced slowly, and it doesn't mean he'll become addicted.

16
00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.338
The other terms.

17
00:00:57.338 --> 00:01:00.316
Tolerance: repeated doses have less effect,

18
00:01:00.316 --> 00:01:03.570
so a bigger dose is needed for the same effect.

19
00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:08.141
Licit means legal, like alcohol or a medicine taken as prescribed.

20
00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:11.396
Illicit means illegal, like every Class A drug.

21
00:01:11.396 --> 00:01:15.481
The antidotes: naloxone for opioids, N A C for paracetamol.

22
00:01:15.481 --> 00:01:21.575
The National Poisons Centre is free, every hour of the day, on oh eight hundred, Poison.

23
00:01:21.575 --> 00:01:27.254
And her rule for that deck: a slide with Pusheen the cat is tested on the concept,

24
00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:28.708
never its statistics.

25
00:01:29.158 --> 00:01:35.106
Dependence: withdrawal symptoms when a drug is stopped abruptly; can be purely medical.

26
00:01:35.106 --> 00:01:40.506
Addiction: a behaviour; overwhelming involvement in getting and using, craving,

27
00:01:40.506 --> 00:01:42.284
use despite harm, relapse.

28
00:01:42.284 --> 00:01:45.155
Tolerance: less effect from the same dose.

29
00:01:45.155 --> 00:01:47.547
Licit is legal, illicit is illegal.

30
00:01:47.547 --> 00:01:50.555
Naloxone for opioids; N A C for paracetamol.
